# Build output
/saint
/dist/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Go test and coverage artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# The developer's own tooling, not the project's.
#
# These describe one person's setup - which agent plugins they run, which
# commands they have permitted locally - and say nothing about how to build or
# use saint. Anyone cloning this repo brings their own.
#
# CLAUDE.md at the root is not covered by this and is deliberately tracked: it
# is instructions for working on saint, not configuration for one machine.
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
# Inputs and state for the Impeccable design tool: its product brief, design
# spec and generated tokens.
.impeccable/
/PRODUCT.md
/DESIGN.md
.aider*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.local.json

# saint's own runtime state.
#
# None of this belongs in a checkout, and all of it is machine-local by
# definition: the state directory records real session IDs and mount paths off
# the developer's filesystem, the journal records every request a guest made,
# and a transcript is a raw dump of an agent's terminal - which is whatever the
# agent was working on. These are listed even though saint writes them under
# ~/.saint, because a redirected home or a test run in the wrong directory is
# exactly the accident this file exists to survive.
/.saint/
/saint.log
/proxy.jsonl
/proxy.jsonl.*
/transcript.log
/sessions/
/tokens/

# Secrets.
#
# saint hands a subscription token to a container through a 0600 env file, and
# writes it to a host temp directory rather than anywhere near the repo. This is
# the second line, not the first: no credential should ever be written here, and
# if one is, it must not become a commit.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.pem
*.key
